.TH FERRENT-CLI 1 "2026-11-23" "ferrent-cli 1.0.0" "Ferrent"
.SH NAME
ferrent-cli \- control a Ferrent daemon over TLS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferrent-cli
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ferrent-cli
talks to the Ferrent daemon's TLS gRPC API. It lists and edits torrents,
manages labels, trackers, limits and saved servers, and imports Deluge state.
Every reading command accepts \fB\-\-json\fR for stable machine output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-server \fIURL|NAME\fR
daemon address (default \fIhttps://127.0.0.1:50051\fR) or a saved profile name
.TP
.B \-\-ca \fIFILE\fR
CA certificate used to pin the daemon
.TP
.B \-\-token \fITOKEN\fR
API token; the daemon generates it on first install
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIFILE\fR
CLI config (default \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ferrent/cli.toml\fR)
.TP
.B \-\-json
machine-readable output
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add
add a .torrent file
.TP
.B list
list torrents with server-side filtering, sorting and paging
.TP
.B show
show one torrent
.TP
.B peers
list the peers of one torrent
.TP
.B status
health summary: version, uptime, torrent counts, free space, TLS pin
.TP
.B stats
session totals: bytes, ratio, peers, uptime
.TP
.B files
list the files of one torrent; \fB\-\-set\fR changes priorities
.TP
.B trackers
list, add or remove announce URLs
.TP
.B webseeds
list or replace the web seeds
.TP
.B labels
list labels; create, update, delete or assign one
.TP
.B limits
set per-torrent rate and connection limits
.TP
.B set
toggle sequential download or super seeding
.TP
.B pause
pause a torrent
.TP
.B resume
resume a torrent
.TP
.B remove
remove a torrent
.TP
.B move
move a torrent in the download queue
.TP
.B recheck
verify the existing data against the hashes
.TP
.B rename-file
rename one file inside a torrent
.TP
.B create
build a .torrent on the daemon host
.TP
.B rss
RSS watcher status; \fB\-\-preview\fR fetches one feed
.TP
.B autoadd
watch directories and their scanner counters; \fB\-\-scan\fR scans now
.TP
.B hooks
hook journal: pending events and the recent runs
.TP
.B blocklist
IP blocklist status; \fB\-\-refresh\fR reloads the sources
.TP
.B disks
storage payload: filesystems, zones and free space
.TP
.B config
read or replace the daemon configuration
.TP
.B notify
notification outbox and a test delivery
.TP
.B servers
saved daemons in cli.toml: list, add, remove, use
.TP
.B import-deluge
import a Deluge state directory (paused adds)
.TP
.B watch
stream torrent deltas until Ctrl-C
.PP
Run
.B ferrent-cli \fICOMMAND\fB \-\-help\fR
for the flags of one command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 runtime, 2 usage/config, 3 not found, 4 auth, 5 transport/TLS.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ferrent/token
token generated by the package's postinst
.TP
.I /var/lib/ferrent/tls-cert.pem
CA certificate the daemon creates on first start
.TP
.I ~/.config/ferrent/cli.toml
client config with saved server profiles (mode 0600)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ferrentd (1),
.BR ferrent-gui (1)
